\title{02 · Root (stage 1)}
\taxon{Chapter}
\meta{origin}{design/02-root.md}
\meta{layer}{human}
\tag{chapter}

\p{The root is the single definition everything else instantiates, together with the constructions that must be made before the seal because they need the kernel: maps, equivalences, fibrant replacement, derived mapping spaces, walking structures and \code{Mod}, \code{Mat(Set)}, \code{Category}, the discrete embedding, and the interface itself.}
\p{Throughout, \code{X : Type u} is a label set and \code{Θ := Θ^aug_{fc,X}} (→ \ref{dec-kr-0006}, \ref{dec-kr-0007}). Elementary shapes: \code{pt(x)}, \code{v(x,y)}, \code{h(x,y)}, \code{c_n(x₀…x_n; y₀,y₁)}, \code{c_n^∅(x₀…x_n; y)}.}
